        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: restore terminal pgrp after PATH lookup",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Launch interactive PATH probes in a detached session so shell startup cannot take ownership of the caller's controlling terminal.\n- Preserve process-group cleanup for timed-out and background shell children; the session leader remains the cleanup group leader.\n- Check spawn-attribute setup, cover the detached-session flag contract, and document the user-visible fix.\n\n## Validation\n- Exact head: `0d7d8e1b1b96bfb8573389efab0ae89e59173af5`.\n- Focused path/foreground suites: 50/50 passed.\n- `make check`: SwiftFormat and SwiftLint clean.\n- Zero-retry full suite: 613/613 selections, 52/52 groups first-pass green, no retries, recoveries, or timeouts.\n- Autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings; 0.93 correctness confidence.\n- Real controlling-PTY proof through public `ShellCommandLocator.commandV`: two concurrent interactive shell probes resolved a PATH exported by shell startup with worker stdin redirected to `/dev/null`; the original foreground group never changed and a literal Ctrl+C byte reached the foreground sentinel.\n- Developer ID-signed debug bundle from exact head passed strict code-sign and Gatekeeper verification; bundled CLI reports CodexBar 0.42.1.\n- Production CodexBar PID, executable path, and start time remained unchanged.\n\n## Risk\nThe change is limited to shell PATH probing. Detached probes still run interactive login-shell initialization, but intentionally have no controlling terminal; terminal-dependent startup prompts can no longer interfere with the caller. Existing noninteractive CI behavior is preserved.\n\n## Dependencies\nNo dependency changes; freshness review not applicable.\n",
